## 🚦 Interactive Connection Control

Little Snitch can notify you when an application attempts a network connection, giving you control over whether that connection should be permitted.

<div style="text-align:left;">

### 🛡️ Connection Decision Workflow

* 🔔 **Connection Alert** — See when an application requests network access.
* 👤 **Identify the Process** — Check which app or process initiated the connection.
* 🌐 **Inspect Destination** — Review the remote server or Internet address.
* ✅ **Allow** — Create or apply a rule that permits the connection.
* 🚫 **Deny** — Block the connection according to your selected rule.
* ⏱️ **Temporary Rule** — Use temporary decisions when permanent rules are unnecessary.
* 🧠 **Remember Choice** — Keep suitable rules for future connections.

---

## 📊 Network Monitor

Network Monitor provides a detailed view of network activity, including current and historical connection information. Little Snitch can retain connection statistics for analysis over periods of up to one year.

<div style="text-align:left;">

| 📈 **Monitoring Tool**  | 🔍 **What You Can Inspect**                  |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| 🌐 **Live Connections** | ⚡ Current network activity                   |
| 📱 **Application**      | 🧩 Which app initiated a connection          |
| 🖥️ **Remote Computer** | 🌍 Destination host information              |
| 🔢 **Internet Address** | 📡 Remote IP address                         |
| 🔌 **Port**             | 🚪 Connection port                           |
| 📡 **Protocol**         | 🔗 Network protocol                          |
| 📤 **Data Transfer**    | 📊 Amount of transferred data                |
| 🛡️ **Rule Coverage**   | 📋 Which rules apply                         |
| 🗺️ **Location Map**    | 🌍 Geographic visualization based on IP data |

</div>

